failures: "2 guarded failure cases\nSee the recorded conditions and effects below" {
  link: "#process/interaction/recovery"
  tooltip: "A selected journal, snapshot, target, action, version, or identity is missing, changed, incompatible, or untrusted; a target matches neither retained side.\nStop recovery without guessing state or replaying actor intent. The advanced wrapper reports recovery-required, except a live writer is busy.\nChecks made before exclusion produce no recovery writes; later rejection may follow private lock/epoch effects. Missing recovery metadata is reported as unavailable, not invented.; A committed journal with an observed before-state target is inconsistent and rejected. Restore is rejected even when a committed journal otherwise validates.\n\nCompletion observes changed declared read basis, or a restore/complete filesystem operation or cleanup is interrupted.\nKeep the actual incomplete or uncertain recovery outcome explicit; reinspection and an explicitly selected current recovery identity are required.\nBefore committed phase, the source may attempt exact guarded restoration after post-publication basis drift. That attempt is not a guarantee that all previous bytes were restored.; After committed phase, no recovery path restores before bytes. Retained evidence and known target identities govern completion/cleanup, not a blind retry."
  style.fill: "#F9EEEE"
  style.stroke: "#597390"
  style.font-color: "#24364A"
  style.font-size: 16
  style.border-radius: 7
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}
